From 5abec3d1fbabca7c4caf0e7340fa21d47ca98aa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junior Mverli <25966843+juniorverli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:01:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] soc: qcom: apr: install the GPR callback before probing
 the client

apr_device_probe() stores the GPR service callback only after the
client probe returned. q6apm sends APM_CMD_GET_SPF_STATE from its probe
and waits for the answer; gpr_do_rx_callback() finds the service but
svc->callback is still NULL, so the response is dropped silently and the
command times out after 5 s:

  qcom-apm gprsvc:service:2:1: CMD timeout for [1001021] opcode

The timeout is not fatal (the return value is ignored) but it delays
the probe by 5 s and leaves apm->state at 0 until a later request.

Install the callback before calling the probe and clear it again when
the probe fails. For APR devices gpr_callback is NULL, so nothing
changes there.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
index ea7f83916..928bac8ef 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
@@ -367,9 +367,16 @@ static int apr_device_probe(struct device *dev)
 	struct apr_driver *adrv = to_apr_driver(dev->driver);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * A GPR client may send a command and wait for the response from its
+	 * probe (q6apm asks for the SPF state). The response needs the
+	 * callback, so install it before the probe runs.
+	 */
+	adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
+
 	ret = adrv->probe(adev);
-	if (!ret)
-		adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
+	if (ret)
+		adev->svc.callback = NULL;
 
 	return ret;
 }
